<!--
  Hero (the commander) and troop characters of Commander Battle's Empire troop classes (cb_mpclassdivisions_empire.xml),
  merged into Native's mpcharacters.xml (MPCharacters, MultiplayerGame only). All new ids: the stock characters stay
  untouched. The rules are those of cb_mpcharacters_vlandia.xml; in short:
  - default_group sets the class group, hence the role (Infantry, Ranged, Cavalry, HorseArcher).
  - Bots draw every equipment slot from a random roster of their character (rolled again per slot), so each slot holds
    the same kind of item in every roster: the rosters vary the looks, never the loadout. Weapons are the same in every
    roster; the weapon setups (perks) swap them.
  - Slots: Item0 main weapon, Item1 shield (or arrows, bolts), Item2 sidearm, Item3 the archers' targe (swapped for a
    pavise by the crossbow setup), otherwise free for a setup's extra (the skirmishers' second bundle of javelins). The
    infantry wear Empire shoulder pieces in the Cape slot, in every roster.
  - Gear tiers: light = levy (padded, a real helmet, a decent shield, a proper weapon); medium = common men-at-arms
    (mail, a good helmet); heavy = palatine guards and cataphracts (lamellar and scale, full helms, the best weapons).
  - Empire doctrine: large kite shields for the infantry of every weight; legionaries are better armoured than other
    cultures' men-at-arms. Archers carry a targe. Cavalry ride with a small round shield or targe and a mace, as RBM's
    cataphracts. Bows are middling (short bow, recurve bow).
  - No throwing weapons in the rosters: Imperial javelins come only with the skirmisher setups.
  - Items only from Native's mpitems.xml.
-->
